{"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"declarations","declarations":[{"languages":["swift"],"platforms":["Linux"],"tokens":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"func"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"resistanceDistance"},{"kind":"text","text":"<"},{"kind":"genericParameter","text":"W"},{"kind":"text","text":">("},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"from"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"internalParam","text":"source"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Self"},{"kind":"text","text":"."},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/Graph\/Vertex","preciseIdentifier":"s:14GraphProtocols0A0P6VertexQa","kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Vertex"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"to"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"internalParam","text":"target"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Self"},{"kind":"text","text":"."},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/Graph\/Vertex","preciseIdentifier":"s:14GraphProtocols0A0P6VertexQa","kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Vertex"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"weight"},{"kind":"text","text":": ("},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Self"},{"kind":"text","text":"."},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/Graph\/Edges-swift.associatedtype","preciseIdentifier":"s:14GraphProtocols0A0P5EdgesQa","kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Edges"},{"kind":"text","text":"."},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:Sl5IndexQa","kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Index"},{"kind":"text","text":") -> "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"W"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"tolerance"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:Sd","kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Double"},{"kind":"text","text":" = 1e-10, "},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"maxIterations"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:Si","kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Int"},{"kind":"text","text":"? = nil) "},{"kind":"keyword","text":"throws"},{"kind":"text","text":"("},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/NoConvergence","preciseIdentifier":"s:14GraphProtocols13NoConvergenceV","kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"NoConvergence"},{"kind":"text","text":") -> "},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:Sd","kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Double"},{"kind":"text","text":"? "},{"kind":"keyword","text":"where"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"W"},{"kind":"text","text":" : "},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:SB","kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"BinaryFloatingPoint"}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"heading","text":"Discussion","level":2,"anchor":"discussion"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Conjugate gradients on the Laplacian grounded at ","type":"text"},{"code":"target","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", from 0, until the residual’s","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"Euclidean norm is at most ","type":"text"},{"code":"tolerance","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" (relative to the right-hand side, which has norm 1),","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"or, on a weight spread that puts that below rounding, until the true residual stops","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"improving. Jacobi preconditioned for 300 iterations, then by a modified incomplete Cholesky","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"factor in maximum-spanning-tree order. O((n + m) √κ) time; about 9 n words, and O(n + m) for","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"the factor when it is built.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"weight","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" gives the conductance of the edge at each position, read once per position (every","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"position, also outside the component); a weight of 0 is no edge.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"aside","style":"note","name":"Precondition","content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":""},{"code":"source","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" and "},{"code":"target","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" are vertices of the graph, every weight is finite and"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"nonnegative, "},{"code":"tolerance > 0","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", and "},{"code":"maxIterations","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", when given, is at least 1."}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"type":"aside","style":"note","name":"Throws","content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"NoConvergence"},{"text":" after ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"maxIterations"},{"text":" conjugate-gradient iterations (one","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"matrix–vector product each; 20,000 + 2n when nil), with that count and the residual’s norm","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"relative to the right-hand side’s. No input has reached the default limit in the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"measurements.","type":"text"}]}]}],"kind":"content"}],"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/SpectralGraphTheory\/documentation\/SpectralGraphTheory","doc:\/\/SpectralGraphTheory\/documentation\/SpectralGraphTheory\/GraphProtocols","doc:\/\/SpectralGraphTheory\/documentation\/SpectralGraphTheory\/GraphProtocols\/Graph"]]},"sections":[],"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/SpectralGraphTheory\/documentation\/SpectralGraphTheory\/GraphProtocols\/Graph\/resistanceDistance(from:to:weight:tolerance:maxIterations:)-4cudc","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The resistance distance between "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"source"},{"type":"text","text":" and "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"target"},{"type":"text","text":" (Klein and Randić 1993): the effective"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"resistance between them when each edge is a conductance (its weight; 1 without "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"weight:"},{"type":"text","text":"),"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"(e_s − e_t)ᵀ L⁺ (e_s − e_t). 0 when they are the same vertex, without reading any weight;"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"nil when they lie in different components. Symmetric. To read weights as resistances"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"instead, pass "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"{ 1 \/ r($0) }"},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/spectralgraphtheory\/graphprotocols\/graph\/resistancedistance(from:to:weight:tolerance:maxiterations:)-4cudc"]}],"kind":"symbol","schemaVersion":{"patch":0,"minor":3,"major":0},"metadata":{"roleHeading":"Instance Method","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"func"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"resistanceDistance"},{"kind":"text","text":"<"},{"kind":"genericParameter","text":"W"},{"kind":"text","text":">("},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"from"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Self"},{"kind":"text","text":"."},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:14GraphProtocols0A0P6VertexQa","text":"Vertex"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"to"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Self"},{"kind":"text","text":"."},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:14GraphProtocols0A0P6VertexQa","text":"Vertex"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"weight"},{"kind":"text","text":": ("},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Self"},{"kind":"text","text":"."},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:14GraphProtocols0A0P5EdgesQa","text":"Edges"},{"kind":"text","text":"."},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:Sl5IndexQa","text":"Index"},{"kind":"text","text":") -> "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"W"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"tolerance"},{"kind":"